# Touch Scrolling Direction: a drag moves lists and conversations the same way. Same (the
# default): the selection and the view move the way the finger does, down is
# toward later items and newer messages. Opposite: the content follows the
# finger, so each goes the other way. A list drag is one row of the list's own height (35 px for chats here), so
# with Opposite the list follows the finger.
vim on
repeat 14 100 rx dm 0 Message number # in a long conversation, long enough to scroll
wait 300
# Conversations first, from an untouched list: tap the top row, drag 60 px each way.
tap 100 40
shot same-chat-start
swipe 160 170 160 110 300
shot same-chat-finger-up
swipe 160 110 160 170 300
shot same-chat-finger-down
tap 10 8
pref scroll opposite
tap 100 40
shot opposite-chat-start
swipe 160 170 160 110 300
shot opposite-chat-finger-up
swipe 160 110 160 170 300
shot opposite-chat-finger-down
tap 10 8
# Lists: from the third row, drag 70 px (two rows) down, then 35 px up.
pref scroll same
key down 2
shot same-list-start
swipe 160 100 160 170 300
shot same-list-finger-down
swipe 160 170 160 135 300
shot same-list-finger-up
pref scroll opposite
key up 2
key down 2
shot opposite-list-start
swipe 160 100 160 170 300
shot opposite-list-finger-down
swipe 160 170 160 135 300
shot opposite-list-finger-up
